{{define "research"}}
<section class="o-hero-page research-hero hard-adoption-hero" aria-labelledby="hard-title">
<div class="research-hero-copy">
<p class="o-hero-page-eyebrow">Public Preview</p>
<h1 class="o-hero-page-title" id="hard-title">H.A.R.D. Protocol 0.2</h1>
<p class="hard-full-name t-body-s">Human-centered AI Readiness and Decision Protocol</p>
<p class="hard-value t-title-xl">Review the choices inside the result.</p>
<p class="t-body-m">AI can deliver a finished-looking product before you have examined the choices inside it. H.A.R.D. works backward from a plan, design or code: what was chosen, which alternatives fit, why it serves the purpose, and what evidence supports it.</p>
<div class="m-cta-pair"><a class="button button-primary" data-primary-task data-entry-route href="#start">Choose a review</a><a class="button button-secondary" data-primary-task data-entry-route id="agent-tools" href="/research/ai-readiness/developers">Protocol Library</a></div>
</div>
<nav class="hard-entry-links" aria-label="More ways to use H.A.R.D.">
<div><span class="t-eyebrow">Get started</span><div class="hard-entry-group"><a class="link" data-entry-route href="#method">How it works</a><a class="link" data-entry-route href="/research/ai-readiness/developers#rules">Find a rule</a></div></div>
<div><span class="t-eyebrow">Use your assistant</span><div class="hard-entry-group"><a class="link" data-entry-route data-open-tool="mcp" href="/research/ai-readiness/developers#setup-mcp">Connect MCP</a><a class="link" data-entry-route href="/static/research/ai-readiness/hard-0.2-preview-3/ai-ready-0.2.0-rc.9.zip" download>Download Skill</a></div></div>
</nav>
<figure class="hard-generated-figure" aria-labelledby="hard-visual-caption">
<img src="/static/research/ai-readiness/visuals/hard-app-review-20260925.jpg" width="1536" height="1024" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" alt="App concept: a request-review interface beside requirement, recovery and evidence prompts, with a receive, review and resolve workflow below.">
<figcaption id="hard-visual-caption" class="t-body-s">A working report screen already contains decisions about waiting, retries, saved state and cost. The review beside it asks why those choices fit the product, what alternatives were considered, and which consequences have actually been checked. The illustration is not a participant record or a working review application.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>

<section class="o-section o-section--bordered" id="method"><div class="o-section-inner hard-method-layout">
<div class="stack stack-4 hard-method-intro">
<p class="t-eyebrow">Research motivation</p>
<h2 class="t-title-xl">Which decisions still need your judgment?</h2>
<p class="t-body-l">Start with an important choice visible in the result. Connect it to the intended outcome, realistic alternatives, benefits and costs, and the evidence for keeping or changing it.</p>
<p class="t-body-m">Separate a recorded earlier rationale from a new explanation. Where a decision remains unconfirmed, identify the human judgment, implementation change or validation needed next. A well-supported existing choice can stay.</p>
<p class="t-body-s">The proposed study has not established an effect. This protocol is a review method, not an image filter or a claim that polished work is defective.</p>
</div>
<div class="stack stack-5 hard-method-review" id="scenarios">
<div class="stack stack-2">
<p class="t-eyebrow">In practice</p>
<h3 class="t-title-l">Follow a choice back to its purpose.</h3>
</div>
<ol class="hard-method-steps t-body-m" role="list">
<li><strong>Keep the original artifact.</strong><p>Review the actual design or code revision. Do not blur labels or remove information people need.</p></li>
<li><strong>Compare alternatives and consequences.</strong><p>Ask why this choice fits the task and constraints. Distinguish documented earlier alternatives from options proposed in this review. Name what the choice gains and gives up.</p></li>
<li><strong>Connect judgment to evidence and action.</strong><p>Record what is specified, walkthrough-checked, implemented and runtime-tested separately. Preserve unknowns, name the human owner and record the next decision or check.</p></li>
</ol>
<p class="t-body-s hard-method-boundary">A separate structure view is optional review guidance, not an extra gate. Keep it separate from the proposed study design.</p>
</div>
</div></section>

<section class="o-section o-section--bordered" id="start"><div class="o-section-inner stack stack-5">
<div class="hard-section-intro"><p class="t-eyebrow">Choose the purpose of your review</p><h2 class="t-title-xl">One protocol. Three ways to use it.</h2><p class="t-body-l">A small team can inspect one artifact now. Add the six-gate review when deciding on an engineering investment, or an independent evaluation when measuring reviewer performance.</p></div>
<div class="hard-use-paths" id="downloads">
<article class="o-card-archetype stack stack-3" data-use-path="artifact"><p class="t-eyebrow">One person or a small team</p><h3 class="t-title-l">Artifact Review</h3><p class="t-body-m">Review choices, requirements and recovery in a plan, prototype or code artifact. Keep the four evidence levels separate.</p><p class="t-body-s">A plan can support a specification handoff. It cannot establish runtime readiness.</p><a class="button button-secondary" data-primary-task href="/research/ai-readiness/artifact-review">Start Artifact Review</a></article>
<article class="o-card-archetype stack stack-3" data-use-path="quick"><p class="t-eyebrow">Bounded engineering investment</p><h3 class="t-title-l">QUICK-6 / Full Profile</h3><p class="t-body-m">Use QUICK-6 for low-risk work with a baseline, or Full Profile for moderate, high or unknown risk.</p><p class="t-body-s">Stop at a failed or missing gate. The 15-minute target remains untested.</p><a class="button button-secondary" data-primary-task href="/research/ai-readiness/quick-6">Open QUICK-6</a><a class="link" href="/research/ai-readiness/full-profile">Open Full Profile</a></article>
<article class="o-card-archetype stack stack-3" data-use-path="independent"><p class="t-eyebrow">Optional evaluator research</p><h3 class="t-title-l">Independent evaluation</h3><p class="t-body-m">Add frozen references, independent roles and locked judgments to examine reviewer performance.</p><p class="t-body-s">Ineligible measures stay N/A with reasons. Agent results remain separate from human results.</p><a class="button button-secondary" data-primary-task href="/research/ai-readiness/independent-evaluation">Read evaluation rules</a></article>
</div>
<details class="hard-detail" id="quick-six"><summary class="t-title-m">Preview the six questions</summary>
<ol class="research-steps hard-six t-body-m">
<li><strong>What happens today?</strong><p>Record the steps, time, failures and rework.</p></li>
<li><strong>What needs to improve, for whom?</strong><p>Tie the requirement to an actual need.</p></li>
<li><strong>What happens when something goes wrong?</strong><p>Define recovery and who may act.</p></li>
<li><strong>What demonstrates the behavior?</strong><p>Trace the requirement to the artifact and its check.</p></li>
<li><strong>What work remains for people?</strong><p>Count review, correction and escalation.</p></li>
<li><strong>Is there enough evidence to fund the next step?</strong><p>Apply the risk depth and name an owner.</p></li>
</ol><p class="hard-stop-note t-body-s"><strong>Stop at a failed or missing gate.</strong> A good answer elsewhere cannot cancel it out. Without a measurable baseline, ROI stays indeterminate.</p></details>
<details class="hard-detail"><summary class="t-title-m">Protocol, worksheets and source files</summary><div class="stack stack-3 t-body-m">
<a class="link" href="/research/ai-readiness/protocol">Read the complete protocol</a>
<a class="link" href="/research/ai-readiness/worksheet">Open the conversation worksheet</a><a class="link" href="/research/ai-readiness/decision-review">Follow the choice review</a><a class="link" href="/research/ai-readiness/pilot">Get the external pilot packet</a>
<a class="link" href="/static/research/ai-readiness/hard-0.2-preview-3/HARD-Protocol-0.2-preview.3.pdf" download>Protocol PDF</a>
<a class="link" href="/static/research/ai-readiness/hard-0.2-preview-3/HARD-QUICK-6-0.2-preview.3.pdf" download>QUICK-6 PDF</a>
<a class="link" href="/static/research/ai-readiness/hard-0.2-preview-3/HARD-Full-Profile-0.2-preview.3.pdf">Full Profile PDF</a>
<a class="link" href="/static/research/ai-readiness/hard-0.2-preview-3/HARD-Protocol-0.2-preview.3.zip">Complete current source package</a>
</div></details>
</div></section>

<section class="o-section o-section--bordered" id="criteria"><div class="o-section-inner stack stack-5">
<div class="hard-section-intro"><p class="t-eyebrow">Look across the work</p><h2 class="t-title-xl">Some questions live outside the interface.</h2><p class="t-body-m">Use these four views to bring the right people into the review. They are discussion aids, not extra gates or separate scores.</p></div>
<div class="o-persona-grid research-role-grid">
<article class="o-persona-card"><div class="o-persona-card-summary"><div class="o-persona-card-head"><span class="m-avatar" aria-hidden="true">01</span><div><h3 class="o-persona-card-name">Experience and information</h3><p class="o-persona-card-role">Can people find their way?</p></div></div><p class="o-persona-card-jtbd">Check labels, information hierarchy and competing choices against the task people need to complete.</p></div></article>
<article class="o-persona-card"><div class="o-persona-card-summary"><div class="o-persona-card-head"><span class="m-avatar" aria-hidden="true">02</span><div><h3 class="o-persona-card-name">Workflow and architecture</h3><p class="o-persona-card-role">Do the handoffs work?</p></div></div><p class="o-persona-card-jtbd">Follow the dependencies and state changes, including what happens when a step fails.</p></div></article>
<article class="o-persona-card"><div class="o-persona-card-summary"><div class="o-persona-card-head"><span class="m-avatar" aria-hidden="true">03</span><div><h3 class="o-persona-card-name">Implementation and evidence</h3><p class="o-persona-card-role">What has been checked?</p></div></div><p class="o-persona-card-jtbd">Distinguish working behavior from simulation. Link each important requirement to a check of the exact artifact.</p></div></article>
<article class="o-persona-card"><div class="o-persona-card-summary"><div class="o-persona-card-head"><span class="m-avatar" aria-hidden="true">04</span><div><h3 class="o-persona-card-name">People and operation</h3><p class="o-persona-card-role">Who handles the remaining work?</p></div></div><p class="o-persona-card-jtbd">Name the people responsible for review, correction and support. Include their time when estimating savings.</p></div></article>
</div>
<div class="hard-legacy-anchors" aria-hidden="true">
